    "<sandbox>/work in argv stands for a scratch copy of the files listed in inputs, mounted read-only; runs/RUN-lean-preservation-frag/inputs/ holds those files as they ran.",
    "Recorded for W1 follow-up 1 (docs/waves/W1-report.md). run@1's task field admits only W<n>-S<nn>/W<n>-T<nn> IDs, so the follow-up is named in task_label instead.",
    "Each log is the container's stdout and stderr, as lean printed them. verdict_lines are the error and warning header lines, the #print axioms lines and the #eval/#check output lines, copied from the log.",
    "Partial record. Covered: the vacuous-compiler proof (S9.L4 cell 2) and S9.L5's post_sim. Not covered, because the artifacts are not built: S9.L6's three cells (they use Outcome, Cmd, runS, exec, exec_append, compE_correct, compPost and runPost from the LAB-9 template), the variants without ∀ regs, pack S9B's reference proof, its comparator and --paranoid runs, and the assembled preservation theorem's axioms (lab.yaml, LAB-9.10). Citations of those stay unbacked until the template exists."
